<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 2.68 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 2.68 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index fell 2.14 points, 2.68 percent, to 77.61 after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index fell 193.12 points to a provisional 3,453.61.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 13.06 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
